{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>For</b> — 'He adds transgression to his sin' [at] every time." "<b>He claps hands among us</b> — excessively, like 'shall one clap hands against dust of Samaria' [1 Kings 20:10]. And the meaning is that which is sufficient among us, but against the Place [i.e., God] he multiplies words."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :register {:flags {1 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:32.327058746Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}